---
/**
 * The arcade toast stack: transient notices a cabinet raises through
 * `createToaster` in src/games/engine/toast.ts, which is the required shared
 * channel for toast *behaviour*. This component is the matching channel for
 * their markup and presentation, so restyling the floor's toasts is one edit
 * rather than one per cabinet.
 *
 * Drop it inside the positioned wrapper that holds the game canvas and its
 * overlays; the game then mounts it with
 * `createToaster(document.getElementById('toast-area'))`. The `.toast`
 * children are created at runtime by that module, never here, which is why
 * their rule is declared with `:global`.
 *
 * Deliberately sets no `z-index`, which leaves each cabinet's stacking exactly
 * as it shipped. Raising the stack above the overlays looks like the obvious
 * fix — a record toast that fires as the game-over panel goes up is spent
 * behind it and never fires again — but measured at a phone width it trades
 * that bug for another: the opaque pill then lands on Line Hold's "Hold Again"
 * button for the toast's full 2.4s. Tank Duel already has that second problem,
 * because PR #251 raised its stack to `z-index: 2` and its own overlay sets
 * none; that one cabinet keeps its rule locally. Which of the two bugs each
 * cabinet should have is a design call, not a CSS one — issue #284 tracks it,
 * and the likely answer is that a terminal overlay should carry the record
 * itself rather than race a toast against it.
 *
 * Long toasts wrap rather than run off. Five of the six copies carried
 * `white-space: nowrap`, which reads as a tidy single-line pill until a
 * localised string is long: `.game-area` is `overflow: hidden`, so at 375px
 * four to six of every cabinet's own toast strings were clipped at both ends
 * in all three locales (Line Hold's Catalan wave-cleared line measured 627px
 * against a 327px area). Wrapping clips none of them.
 */
---

<div id="toast-area" class="toast-area"></div>

<style>
  .toast-area {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: var(--space-md);
    /* Spans the field rather than the old `left: 50%` + `translateX(-50%)`,
       which is not equivalent once toasts wrap: an absolutely positioned
       shrink-to-fit box offset from the left edge gets only the remaining half
       as its available width, so a long toast collapsed to a 162px, four-line
       sliver. Anchored to both edges the pill can use the full width and the
       flex centring keeps it where it was. */
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    padding: 0 var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .toast-area :global(.toast) {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: 999px;
    animation: toastIn 0.2s ease;
    max-width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @keyframes toastIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
</style>
